#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:5
#: 48b9d05133704c138439287d0edb80bc
msgid "Thrust Loss and Yaw Imbalance Warnings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:7
#: 93237f8bb6a84641b73ee564b28c6f8f
msgid ""
"If you see thrust loss or yaw imbalance warnings this page outlines some "
"checks and modifications that should be done to resolve the issue. In the"
" majority of cases these warnings are the result of incorrect hardware "
"selection or setup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:9
#: 8b4655b793014598a06792137dd94f14
msgid ""
"These warnings are designed to detect hardware failures in the propulsion"
" system. If they begin to occur on a vehicle that has been flying without"
" warnings the propulsion system should be checked. Warnings are more "
"likely to occur with larger payloads and in strong/gusty winds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:13
#: 4534273c4c6d4aa68026b7b92a636ccd
msgid "Potential Thrust Loss"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:15
#: a872ece22bb24b3098f35976c9a2fb43
msgid ""
"If potential thrust loss messages are seen either on GCS or in the data-"
"flash logs, then an investigation should be done to find the cause and "
"remedy. The warning will give a motor number, for example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:17
#: 9509b0a1117d46a5ba9a3e91f5bc52f9
msgid "```Potential Thrust Loss (3)```"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:19
#: 2f5b1ded9a754acda0d1774e7a83b6c1
msgid ""
"These warnings are the result of a motor or motors saturating at 100% "
"throttle. Because of this saturation ArduCopter can no longer achieve the"
" requested roll, pitch, yaw and throttle output. If this continues for a "
"prolonged period of time the vehicle will have reduced altitude and "
"attitude control and may crash."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:22
#: 66764eaeb7f64b40bb3c633fcc1ac4d1
msgid ""
"If these messages are seen in hover or relaxed flight, the problem must "
"be fixed in hardware. The vehicle's thrust to weight ratio should be "
"increased, either by a change in propulsion or reduction in mass."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:24
#: a70c8230685843ee9654895c9d24b31b
msgid ""
"If only seen in climbing and aggressive maneuvers it may be sufficient to"
" lower the requested accelerations and speeds. Again the vehicle's thrust"
" to weight ratio can be increased to allow higher accelerations and "
"speeds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:29
#: a86f18c5dd82431abc6a03f7fff56a3b
msgid "Yaw Imbalance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:31
#: 989b377d52cb4006994d759dd3f2c29c
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The yaw imbalance warning is a measure of how hard the vehicle is working"
" to yaw, the warning will trigger before the yaw output is saturated. If "
"the yaw output becomes saturated the vehicle's ability to maintain yaw "
"will be compromised. And, in the worst case, this will result in the "
"vehicle rapidly spinning. The warning message gives a percentage of "
"maximum yaw output. At 100% it is saturated. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:34
#: 30869760b2904659937f418c1240de6a
msgid "```Yaw Imbalance 87%```"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:36
#: 46010cef17c942f098ce7d82e390474f
msgid ""
"If seen in hover, the issue should be resolved in hardware. If the value "
"is increasing with no pilot yaw input, the vehicle should be landed "
"immediately. Yaw imbalance can be recognized in dataflash logs by "
"comparing the PWM outputs between pars of opposing motors. It will "
"present as a large throttle level difference between the clockwise and "
"counter clockwise motors, as shown below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:42
#: 8615a607129741c2ba35ba289bea94f9
msgid ""
"This should be fixed in hardware. The most common cause is the motors not"
" being vertical on a circular arm. If the imbalance still persists the "
"motors can be tilted slightly such that the thrust angle assists the yaw "
"for its rotation direction. Some vehicles can be extremely sensitive to "
"motors thrust vector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:45
#: 74461a718ea148d98ffe54838a1c4565
msgid ""
"If the warning is only seen in aggressive yaw maneuvers, the warning "
"threshold can be increased by raising "
":ref:`ATC_RAT_YAW_IMAX<ATC_RAT_YAW_IMAX__AC_AttitudeControl_Multi>`.  "
"However, it may also be worth revisiting the yaw tune."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:48
#: 4c4f3cf44eef4b9c8731573733463a51
msgid ""
"Both the thrust loss and yaw imbalance warnings can be disabled with the "
":ref:`FLIGHT_OPTIONS<FLIGHT_OPTIONS>` parameter. This should only be done"
" after extensive log review and testing to verify the warnings are not "
"picking up genuine issues."
msgstr ""

